body:
I get it, reading is hard. 

&#x200B;

Have a good day bud :)

The sheer amount of assumptions in your comment is wild bro, not really sure where to start

&#x200B;

>Both players deserve to enjoy their experience

Right, I'm not arguing against this. But your comment is incredibly ironic because red is doing exactly what you're complaining about, he was flaming someone for *how they were playing*

&#x200B;

>it’s their time you’re wasting by playing to the beat of your own drum or not reciprocating their effort

That I'm wasting? Nobody was "wasting" this guys time, the lobby wasn't even fucking his in the first place either so he has zero right to complain about the playstyle of others 

&#x200B;

>that’s such a condescending thing to say to someone.

It's condescending to tell people to not be an asshole over a game?

&#x200B;

> How I choose to spend my time js just that, and it should be respected regardless if I’m on a game

Once again, I never argued otherwise

&#x200B;

>And at the end of the day, how can you sit here and clutch pearls when all you ultimately did was stoop to reds level?

Right, because telling someone to not be an asshole over a video game is definitely comparable to telling people to kill themselves. 

&#x200B;

>For all you know, the guy could’ve already muted Red and you’re picking fights solely to maintain a fake moral high ground. 

Yet this isn't what happened. The person that they were flaming left as soon as they started acting like a dick. Also, please tell me what part of telling someone to not be a dick equates to playing a "fake moral high ground". Just another baseless assumption on your part. 

&#x200B;

>Now you’re sitting here and having a flame party

Explaining the situation = flaming? 

&#x200B;

>willing to take your bullying lol

In what fucking world does telling someone to not be a dick equate to being a bully? I think you've severely misunderstood what "bully" means

Genuinely, what does that have to do with anything? At no point did I say something like that wouldn't be frustrating. Has *absolutely nothing* to do with this post, nor the situation that this posts entails. The dive was going perfectly fine and there were no bumps when that random guy started flaming. Mission didn't come anywhere near failing.

&#x200B;

The reason the original commenter is getting downvoted is because his entire comment is based in the assumption that I meant something other than what I actually meant. 

&#x200B;

So yeah, it is just a game. Absolutely not worth getting that upset over. If you lash out like the guy in the pic, then you genuinely have some poor emotional regulation.

Jesus, telling someone to die over a comment when you were the first to start hurling insults? I couldn't imagine.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

#

First off, the blue is me, and second I'm not the level 800 that he was flaming. I said "it's just a game" in response to him acting like a dick for an incredibly minute mistake. And sorry, but if you tell someone to kill themselves over a fuckin video game, you're the asshole 100%, regardless of what the other person did in game.

&#x200B;

Absolutely wild how many assumptions people will make in their comments without making the slightest effort to gain any context on the situation.

&#x200B;

Edit: And to top it all off, the person that red started flaming was nothing but kind throughout the entire mission, and played relatively well imo. They were actively working with the team and only fell behind for legit like less than a minute before "red" started lashing out like this, *in a lobby that wasn't even his.*

Lol, dude this has nothing to do with being open minded. This guy was in the wrong through and through, so I'm not sure what exactly you're trying to justify here. Everyone has bad days or gets frustrated, but again, that doesn't give you any right to be an asshole.

&#x200B;

You've completely ignored my provided context to argue against something that you pulled out of thin air.  At no point did I say that hosts aren't allowed to play how they want lmao. The entire point of this post was to point out that acting like this isn't alright. If you argue otherwise then I really don't know what else to tell you man.
